{"t": 1795076091.8420258, "tool": "analyze", "code": "from scipy.optimize import curve_fit\nfor lo in [2,3,4,5]:\n    m=(T>=lo)&(T<lo+1)\n    f=lambda e,a,b,n,c: a+b*e**n+c*(0)\n    p,_=curve_fit(f,eps[m],sigma[m]-0*T[m],p0=[10,3,.5,0],maxfev=20000)\n    print(lo,p, np.std(sigma[m]-f(eps[m],*p)))\n    # with T linear\n    g=lambda X,a,b,n,c: a+c*X[1]+b*X[0]**n\n    p,_=curve_fit(g,(eps[m],T[m]),sigma[m],p0=[1,3,.5,3],maxfev=20000)\n    print(p,np.std(sigma[m]-g((eps[m],T[m]),*p)))", "out": "2 [12.85116562  0.37121745  1.4866864   0.        ] 0.7730455018806296\n[5.0072753  0.80860567 1.04918349 2.85159368] 0.0636176421529809\n3 [15.53289297  0.71448107  1.01204271  0.        ] 0.8985260896462185\n[4.95614957 0.36383856 1.39040007 3.10825051] 0.11524677681404463\n4 [20.16179003  0.04913946  2.31230186  0.        ] 1.0322914511361423\n[3.52044017 0.042186   2.39093217 3.6699067 ] 0.19143863456513957\n5 [22.45257005  2.45311082 -0.35334842  0.        ] 1.2662771192527948\n[ 4.59529872e+03 -4.59389106e+03  9.39807559e-05  4.28220073e+00] 0.40286226520497526\n\n[stderr]\n<string>:8: OptimizeWarning: Covariance of the parameters could not be estimated\n"}
